markdown <<MARKDOWN
<h1>Reusable Routine: How to Test AI-Generated Loop Code</h1>

When students receive loop code from AI, encourage them to test it systematically. This routine helps students build debugging habits and develop confidence in evaluating AI-generated solutions.


## Loop Verification Checklist 

<div style="background:#F5F7F8;border-radius:14px;padding:24px;margin:24px 0;">

  <div style="display:flex;align-items:flex-start;margin-bottom:18px;">
    <div style="background:#0093A4;color:white;border-radius:50%;width:36px;height:36px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-weight:bold;font-size:16pt;margin-right:16px;">
      1
    </div>
    <div>
      <strong style="font-size:15pt;">First Value Test</strong><br>
      Does the loop start where expected?
    </div>
  </div>

  <div style="display:flex;align-items:flex-start;margin-bottom:18px;">
    <div style="background:#0093A4;color:white;border-radius:50%;width:36px;height:36px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-weight:bold;font-size:16pt;margin-right:16px;">
      2
    </div>
    <div>
      <strong style="font-size:15pt;">Last Value Test</strong><br>
      Does it stop at the correct final value?
    </div>
  </div>

  <div style="display:flex;align-items:flex-start;margin-bottom:18px;">
    <div style="background:#0093A4;color:white;border-radius:50%;width:36px;height:36px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-weight:bold;font-size:16pt;margin-right:16px;">
      3
    </div>
    <div>
      <strong style="font-size:15pt;">Edge Test</strong><br>
      What happens at the boundary?
    </div>
  </div>

  <div style="display:flex;align-items:flex-start;margin-bottom:18px;">
    <div style="background:#0093A4;color:white;border-radius:50%;width:36px;height:36px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-weight:bold;font-size:16pt;margin-right:16px;">
      4
    </div>
    <div>
      <strong style="font-size:15pt;">Extra Iteration Check</strong><br>
      Does the loop accidentally run one extra time?
    </div>
  </div>

  <div style="display:flex;align-items:flex-start;margin-bottom:18px;">
    <div style="background:#0093A4;color:white;border-radius:50%;width:36px;height:36px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-weight:bold;font-size:16pt;margin-right:16px;">
      5
    </div>
    <div>
      <strong style="font-size:15pt;">Missing Iteration Check</strong><br>
      Does it stop too early?
    </div>
  </div>

  <div style="display:flex;align-items:flex-start;">
    <div style="background:#0093A4;color:white;border-radius:50%;width:36px;height:36px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-weight:bold;font-size:16pt;margin-right:16px;">
      6
    </div>
    <div>
      <strong style="font-size:15pt;">Match Check</strong><br>
      Does the output actually match the requested behavior?
    </div>
  </div>

</div>

<div style="background-color:#B7E0E5;border-radius:40px;color:#000000;width:95%;padding:18px 24px;margin:24px 0;">

<p style="font-size:14px;line-height:1.5;margin:0;">
<b>💡 Teacher Tip:</b> Encourage participants to use this routine every time they receive AI-generated loop code. Consistent use builds debugging habits, strengthens understanding of loop boundaries, and reinforces that AI-generated code should always be verified rather than accepted automatically.
</p>

</div>

## Next up

Let's practice using the checklist to debug a loop. 
MARKDOWN
